WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.980
We are honoring extraordinary moms all week long.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.180
And one of them is Clarissa Joi.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.810
She had it all, two degrees, a successful career

4
00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.870
and a family,

5
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.950
and then all that changed when she got divorced.

6
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.650
And then she quickly turned that fear into confidence

7
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.610
and launched this very successful non-profit called

8
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.310
Rise Up Single Mom,

9
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:28.530
and it supports countless single moms all over the country.

10
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.661
And Clarissa is here now to talk about it with us.

11
00:00:31.661 --> 00:00:32.673
(audience applauding)

12
00:00:32.673 --> 00:00:33.506
Welcome Clarissa Joi.

13
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.077
Hi Drew, wow, I can't believe I'm here.

14
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.990
I was so excited to talk to you, I'm a single mom

15
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:48.070
so I was very interested in your story.

16
00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.070
What compelled you to help other women not feel alone?

17
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.670
It started with a simple Facebook post,

18
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.620
it was the end of 2016,

19
00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.140 line:15%
and I was looking back over the year and I was so excited

20
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.700 line:15%
that I was okay as a single mom,

21
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.250
after going through so much darkness

22
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.320
and I just simply wanted to share that with other moms.

23
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.130
And then the responses just poured in,

24
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.570
of other moms thanking me for the post,

25
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.210
and I was like, wow.

26
00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.813
Where did this come from?

27
00:01:18.813 --> 00:01:21.590
And then fast forward in 2017

28
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:25.400
we started the nonprofit organization Rise Up Single Mom.

29
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.590
Is it true that you kept your divorce

30
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.620
a secret from people in the beginning?

31
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.100
Absolutely, I actually even wore my wedding ring

32
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.650
a year after the divorce, simply because

33
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.820
I didn't want to feel like a failure

34
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.770
and I didn't want people to think that I was a failure

35
00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.480
and you know, well, how good can she be in other areas

36
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.020
if now her marriage has failed?

37
00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.010
Absolutely.

38
00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.100
That's it.

39
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.240
If you can't figure out marriage,

40
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.300
then they probably can't figure out anything else.

41
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.537
Absolutely, that's what I was thinking.

42
00:01:55.537 --> 00:01:58.130
That's why I didn't want to share it.

43
00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:01.950
That is one of the most honest, poignant ways

44
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.240
I've gotten to put how divorce feels with another woman.

45
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.670
It's like, you are convinced that others will look at you

46
00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.400
as if it has a trickle down effect to everything.

47
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.010
Absolutely, this paranoia just going on in your head,

48
00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.060
and despite whether others think that way or not,

49
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.710
it's your reality of how you're feeling inside.

50
00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.060
So like what do you say to other mothers

51
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.700
watching right now who are raising their kids on their own

52
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.020
and feeling any of the things we have mentioned?

53
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.970
I would say to other moms it's okay.

54
00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.620
There are others that feel exactly as you do

55
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.620
and just as I was there, you also can come from that place,

56
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.760
you will be okay, this is only a season.

57
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.490
You'll get through it.

58
00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.450
Clarissa, where were you when I first got divorced?

59
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.140
I'm serious.

60
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.700
Thank goodness that you have been such an inspiration

61
00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.530
to so many moms,

62
00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.530
and today our virtual audience is filled with single moms.

63
00:03:02.695 --> 00:03:04.136
(audience clapping)

64
00:03:04.136 --> 00:03:05.158
So hello ladies.

65
00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:06.550
I know, how cool is that?

66
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:07.980
There's actually someone here

67
00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.423
who has a special message for you, Tanya, are you there?

68
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.520
Hi Drew, hi Clarissa?

69
00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.827
Hi, Tanya, thank you for joining us today.

70
00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:21.660
How are you?

71
00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.493
Good, how are you?

72
00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.160
Listen, I'm so excited to be here.

73
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.540
Really just thrilled I wanted to say to Clarissa,

74
00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.540
thank you so much for founding Rise Up Single Mom.

75
00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.470
The first time that I actually met with the organization,

76
00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.850
it was a Moms Go Back to School event.

77
00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.860
And I remember Clarissa clearly saying

78
00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:50.640
begin with the end in mind, and that always stuck with me.

79
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.820
And I'm here today to say that

80
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.400
we registered for school that day.

81
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.620
I registered for my master's degree

82
00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.260
at the University of Memphis.

83
00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.500
I have completed all of the classes,

84
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.590 line:15%
except for one class that starts in July.

85
00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.440 line:15%
And I just want to say thank you Clarissa

86
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.200 line:15%
for the catalyst that helped me

87
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.744
through those tiny steps to get to my success.

88
00:04:13.744 --> 00:04:14.577
(audience clapping)

89
00:04:14.577 --> 00:04:15.757
So thank you again.

90
00:04:15.757 --> 00:04:17.940
I am so thankful and grateful for this organization.

91
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.330
All the amazing moms in our audience,

92
00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.520
we want to celebrate you

93
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.060
by giving you each a hundred dollars gift certificate

94
00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.980
to UrbanStems Flowers,

95
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.440
a company that I really, really really love

96
00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.730
and Clarissa you're just so inspiring,

97
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.130
and we at the show would love to just give $5,000

98
00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.190
towards Rise Up Single Mom

99
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.200
and it's your mission,

100
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.810
it's hard to put into words what you're doing,

101
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.550
but you do wonder if people think you're

102
00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.810
incapable of handling other parts of your life,

103
00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.360
if you couldn't handle this,

104
00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.490
and I just think what you're doing is amazing,

105
00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.210
and very necessary.

106
00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.960
Wow, I just can't say thank you enough.

107
00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.630
This is so truly amazing.

108
00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.720
Well, I thank you to our VFFs for coming

109
00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.830
and showing up for Clarissa, Tanya

110
00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.120
thank you so much,

111
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.850 line:15%
and go to our website to learn more about Rise Up Single Mom

112
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:22.820 line:15%
an organization that I cannot advocate, support

113
00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.200
and shine a light on more.

114
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.083
Thank you, Clarissa Joi so much.

115
00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:30.666 line:15%
(upbeat music)

